        <mxCell id="08vikgOqioZN39U6YDpm-1" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Add Service Ticket&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1430" y="30" width="250" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08vikgOqioZN39U6YDpm-3" value="&lt;font&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Service Tickets differ from proramming tickets in several ways. One such is that a Service Ticket is not a collection of tasks. It is a single request, either to purchase things like gages, or else to service (repair, calibrate, etc.) a piece of metrology equipment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Form-level permissions are not set on this form. User must supply their Employee ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Submittor can choose one or more users to be copied on all emails.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;Service Types&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;- CMM Down&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Other Machine Down (MicroVu, Keyence, etc.)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Gaging (request for purchase)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Calibration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1360" y="80" width="320" height="230" as="geometry" />
